"/concat-stream/)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concat-stream_readme.md:7
msgid "NPM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concat-stream_readme.md:9
msgid "description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concat-stream_readme.md:11
msgid ""
"Streams emit many buffers. If you want to collect all of the buffers, and"
" when the stream ends concatenate all of the buffers together and receive"
" a single buffer then this is the module for you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concat-stream_readme.md:13
msgid ""
"Only use this if you know you can fit all of the output of your stream "
"into a single Buffer (e.g. in RAM)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concat-stream_readme.md:15
msgid ""
"There are also `objectMode` streams that emit things other than Buffers, "
"and you can concatenate these too. See below for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concat-stream_readme.md:17
msgid "Related"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concat-stream_readme.md:19
msgid ""
"`concat-stream` is part of the [mississippi stream utility "
"collection](https://github.com/maxogden/mississippi) which includes more "
"useful stream modules similar to this one."
msgstr ""

