#: ../../source/concat-stream_readme.md:76
#, python-brace-format
msgid "var writable = concat(opts={}, cb)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concat-stream_readme.md:78
msgid ""
"Return a `writable` stream that will fire `cb(data)` with all of the data"
" that was written to the stream. Data can be written to `writable` as "
"strings, Buffers, arrays of byte integers, and Uint8Arrays."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concat-stream_readme.md:82
msgid ""
"By default `concat-stream` will give you back the same data type as the "
"type of the first buffer written to the stream. Use `opts.encoding` to "
"set what format `data` should be returned as, e.g. if you if you don't "
"want to rely on the built-in type checking or for some other reason."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concat-stream_readme.md:84
msgid "`string` - get a string"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concat-stream_readme.md:85
msgid "`buffer` - get back a Buffer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concat-stream_readme.md:86
msgid "`array` - get an array of byte integers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concat-stream_readme.md:87
msgid "`uint8array`, `u8`, `uint8` - get back a Uint8Array"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concat-stream_readme.md:88
msgid "`object`, get back an array of Objects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concat-stream_readme.md:90
msgid ""
"If you don't specify an encoding, and the types can't be inferred (e.g. "
"you write things that aren't in the list above), it will try to convert "
"concat them into a `Buffer`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concat-stream_readme.md:92
msgid ""
"If nothing is written to `writable` then `data` will be an empty array "
"`[]`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concat-stream_readme.md:94
msgid "error handling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concat-stream_readme.md:96
msgid ""
"`concat-stream` does not handle errors for you, so you must handle errors"
" on whatever streams you pipe into `concat-stream`. This is a general "
"rule when programming with node.js streams: always handle errors on each "
"and every stream. Since `concat-stream` is not itself a stream it does "
"not emit errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/concat-stream_readme.md:98
msgid ""
"We recommend using [`end-of-stream`](https://npmjs.org/end-of-stream) or "
"[`pump`](https://npmjs.org/pump) for writing error tolerant stream code."
msgstr ""

